--[[
    fihware UI Library  v2.0
    Research-backed, bug-aware Roblox UI library

    Key architectural decisions (all research-driven):

    DRAGGING
      MouseButton1 InputObjects do NOT update their .Position after creation.
      Correct pattern: store dragStart on InputBegan, set dragInput from
      frame.InputChanged (MouseMovement object, which IS live), then read
      position in UserInputService.InputChanged.

    SCROLLINGFRAME + UIPADDING
      AutomaticCanvasSize + UIPadding on the same ScrollingFrame = broken
      (padding scales off AbsoluteCanvasSize, not AbsoluteSize).
      Fix: UIPadding lives on an INNER Frame inside the ScrollingFrame.
      CanvasSize is driven manually from UIListLayout.AbsoluteContentSize.

    UICORNER + CLIPSDESCENDANTS
      ClipsDescendants clips at the rectangular boundary, ignoring UICorner.
      Children "spill out" at rounded corners. Never rely on ClipsDescendants
      for rounded clipping. Use ClipsDescendants only on non-rounded containers.

    ZINDEXBEHAVIOR
      Sibling: children always render above parent, no global ZIndex arithmetic.
      Use DisplayOrder on the ScreenGui for overall layering vs other UIs.

    TWEENS
      Cache TweenInfo objects — don't recreate them per call.
      Never tween Visible (boolean, not tweenable).
      Use TextTransparency alongside BackgroundTransparency for text fades.

    NOTIFICATIONS
      UIListLayout on a dynamic notification holder causes reflow jank as items
      are added/removed. Use absolute UDim2.fromOffset positioning instead.
]]

local TweenService     = game:GetService("TweenService")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")
local Players          = game:GetService("Players")

local fihware = {}
fihware.__index = fihware

